  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 211 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nRemnants of Isaias are slowly making their way into and through \neastern portions of the CWA today and tonight. Wind gust potential \nhas continued to trend down slightly w/gusts of 20-25 mph possible. \nRain totals have trended down as well. The highest totals are around \n0.5\" over the southeast Pennyrile and decrease as you move north and \nwest. Rain will taper off west to east overnight. Skies will also \nclear west to east tomorrow throughout the day. \n\nWarmer temperatures return with the clearing skies tomorrow and will \nremain above normal through Thursday. There is a good chance of \nrecord highs on Tuesday (the warmest day of the week) and even some \nrecord warm lows. The pattern then becomes more unsettled mid to \nlate week. 20-50% rain chances return Wednesday and continue in a \ngradual decline through Friday morning. A cold front looks to come \nthrough Thursday night and brings temperatures back down for the \nweekend closer to normal.",
